(1654, 'Consider the following statements: S1: Boolean expressions and logic networks correspond to labeled acrylic digraphs. S2: Optimal Boolean expressions may not correspond to simplest networks. S3: Choosing essential blocks first in a Karnaugh map and then greedily choosing the largest remaining blocks to cover may not give an optimal expression. Which of these statements(s) is/are correct?', NULL, '[\"S1 only\", \"S2 only\", \"S1 and S2\", \"S1, S2 and S3\"]', 3, 'Computer Science & Engineering', NULL, NULL, 2026, 'verified', NULL, 'quality_reviewer_subagent', '2026-09-09 15:11:21', '2026-09-09 15:11:21', 1, 'lt-cs-155-157', 'Consider the following statements: S1: Boolean expressions and logic networks correspond to labeled acrylic digraphs. S2: Optimal Boolean expressions may not correspond to simplest networks. S3: Choosing essential blocks first in a Karnaugh map and then greedily choosing the largest remaining blocks to cover may not give an optimal expression. Which of these statements(s) is/are correct?', 'auto_cleaned', 1, '[]', '2026-09-11T03:14:33.318006+00:00', '2.0.0', 'none'),
