(3033, 'An operating system supports a paged virtual memory, using a central processor with a cycle time of one microsecond. It costs an additional one microsecond to access a page other than the current one. Pages have 1000 words, and the paging device is a drum that rotates at 3000 revolutions per minute and transfers one million words per second. Further, one percent of all instructions executed accessed a page other than the current page. The instruction that accessed another page, 80% accessed a page already in memory and when a new page was required, the replaced page was modified 50% of the time. What is the effective access time on this system, assuming that the system is running only one process and the processor is idle during drum transfers?', NULL, '[\"30 microseconds\",\"34 microseconds\",\"60 microseconds\",\"68 microseconds\"]', 1, 'Computer Science & Engineering', NULL, NULL, 2026, 'verified', NULL, 'quality_reviewer_subagent', '2026-09-09 15:11:21', '2026-09-09 15:11:21', 1, NULL, 'An operating system supports a paged virtual memory, using a central processor with a cycle time of one microsecond. It costs an additional one microsecond to access a page other than the current one. Pages have 1000 words, and the paging device is a drum that rotates at 3000 revolutions per minute and transfers one million words per second. Further, one percent of all instructions executed accessed a page other than the current page. The instruction that accessed another page, 80% accessed a page already in memory and when a new page was required, the replaced page was modified 50% of the time. What is the effective access time on this system, assuming that the system is running only one process and the processor is idle during drum transfers?', 'unchanged', 1, '[]', '2026-09-11T03:14:33.318006+00:00', '1.0.0', 'none'),
